{
  "$schema": "https://agent-plugins.org/schemas/1.0.0/plugin.schema.json",
  "name": "databases",
  "version": "0.1.13",
  "extensions": {
    "dev.sailry.platform": {
      "api_version": "v1",
      "actions": [
        "databases.read",
        "databases.control",
        "databases.manage",
        "conversation.read",
        "conversation.control",
        "projects.read",
        "ssh.read"
      ],
      "display": {
        "label": "Databases",
        "locales": {
          "zh-CN": "数据库"
        },
        "icon": "reicon:ui/database"
      },
      "description": {
        "label": "Connect to databases and run queries",
        "locales": {
          "zh-CN": "连接数据库与执行查询"
        }
      },
      "host": {
        "entry": "dev.sailry.platform/host/main.js",
        "resources": [
          "dev.sailry.platform/host/main.js",
          "dev.sailry.platform/host/tools.js",
          "dev.sailry.platform/host/connections.js"
        ],
        "handlers": [
          "initialize",
          "catalog",
          "query",
          "execute",
          "connections",
          "save",
          "saved"
        ],
        "turn": {
          "initialize": "initialize"
        }
      },
      "tools": [
        {
          "name": "database_catalog",
          "presentation": "summary",
          "description": "List databases, or tables in a selected database, using a saved connection. Credentials remain on the execution Node.",
          "contexts": [
            "workspace",
            "database"
          ],
          "handler": {
            "name": "catalog",
            "operation": "databases.catalog",
            "parameters": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "connection": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{8}(-[0-9a-f]{4}){3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$",
                  "description": "[]"
                },
                "database": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "Database name; omit to use the saved default"
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "connection"
              ],
              "additionalProperties": false
            }
          },
          "display": {
            "label": "Database catalog",
            "locales": {
              "zh-CN": "数据库目录",
              "zh-TW": "資料庫目錄",
              "ja": "データベース一覧",
              "ko": "데이터베이스 목록",
              "fr": "Catalogue des bases de données",
              "de": "Datenbankkatalog",
              "es": "Catálogo de bases de datos",
              "pt-BR": "Catálogo de bancos de dados",
              "ru": "Каталог баз данных",
              "en": "Database catalog"
            },
            "icon": "reicon:ui/database",
            "input": {
              "summary": {
                "path": "/database",
                "code": true
              },
              "content": {
                "path": "/sql",
                "code": true
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "database_query",
          "presentation": "content",
          "description": "Run one read-only SQL statement without approval. The execution connection is forced read-only. Use this for SELECT, inspecting schema, and analysis. Results also appear in the database workspace. Use database_execute for writes; never try to disable read-only protection.",
          "contexts": [
            "workspace",
            "database"
          ],
          "handler": {
            "name": "query",
            "operation": "databases.query",
            "parameters": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "connection": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{8}(-[0-9a-f]{4}){3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$",
                  "description": "[]"
                },
                "database": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "Database name; omit to use the saved default"
                },
                "sql": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "connection",
                "sql"
              ],
              "additionalProperties": false
            }
          },
          "display": {
            "label": "Query database",
            "locales": {
              "zh-CN": "查询数据库",
              "zh-TW": "查詢資料庫",
              "ja": "データベースを照会",
              "ko": "데이터베이스 조회",
              "fr": "Interroger la base de données",
              "de": "Datenbank abfragen",
              "es": "Consultar base de datos",
              "pt-BR": "Consultar banco de dados",
              "ru": "Запрос к базе данных",
              "en": "Query database"
            },
            "icon": "reicon:ui/database",
            "input": {
              "summary": {
                "path": "/database",
                "code": true
              },
              "content": {
                "path": "/sql",
                "code": true
              }
            },
            "output": {
              "table": {
                "columns": {
                  "source": "result",
                  "path": "/data/data/columns"
                },
                "rows": {
                  "source": "result",
                  "path": "/data/data/rows"
                },
                "truncated": {
                  "source": "result",
                  "path": "/data/data/truncated"
                },
                "cell": {
                  "value": "/value",
                  "missing": "NULL",
                  "bytes": "hex"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "database_execute",
          "presentation": "details",
          "description": "Execute one SQL write statement under the session permission policy. Use for INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, and schema changes. For a missing writable SQLite file, an authorized schema write initializes it and creates missing parent directories; do not create the folder or an empty file separately. Explicit writable connection checks can also initialize a missing file. Reads, catalog, read-only connection checks, and PRAGMAs do not initialize a file. The saved connection's read-only setting still applies. Invoke this tool directly instead of asking for approval in chat. Do not retry a denied or uncertain write automatically.",
          "contexts": [
            "workspace",
            "database"
          ],
          "handler": {
            "name": "execute",
            "operation": "databases.execute",
            "parameters": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "connection": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{8}(-[0-9a-f]{4}){3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$",
                  "description": "[]"
                },
                "database": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "Database name; omit to use the saved default"
                },
                "sql": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "connection",
                "sql"
              ],
              "additionalProperties": false
            }
          },
          "display": {
            "label": "Execute SQL",
            "locales": {
              "zh-CN": "执行 SQL",
              "zh-TW": "執行 SQL",
              "ja": "SQL を実行",
              "ko": "SQL 실행",
              "fr": "Exécuter du SQL",
              "de": "SQL ausführen",
              "es": "Ejecutar SQL",
              "pt-BR": "Executar SQL",
              "ru": "Выполнить SQL",
              "en": "Execute SQL"
            },
            "icon": "reicon:ui/database",
            "input": {
              "summary": {
                "path": "/database",
                "code": true
              },
              "content": {
                "path": "/sql",
                "code": true
              }
            },
            "output": {
              "table": {
                "columns": {
                  "source": "result",
                  "path": "/data/data/columns"
                },
                "rows": {
                  "source": "result",
                  "path": "/data/data/rows"
                },
                "truncated": {
                  "source": "result",
                  "path": "/data/data/truncated"
                },
                "cell": {
                  "value": "/value",
                  "missing": "NULL",
                  "bytes": "hex"
                }
              },
              "preview": {
                "parts": [
                  {
                    "text": "affected_rows: ",
                    "when": {
                      "all": [
                        {
                          "value": {
                            "source": "result",
                            "path": "/data/data/affected_rows"
                          },
                          "equals": null,
                          "negate": true
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": {
                      "source": "result",
                      "path": "/data/data/affected_rows"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "database_connections",
          "presentation": "summary",
          "description": "List saved database connections available to this session, including IDs, revisions, engines and whether credentials are required. No passwords are returned.",
          "contexts": [
            "workspace",
            "database"
          ],
          "handler": {
            "name": "connections",
            "operation": "databases.connections",
            "parameters": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {},
              "required": [],
              "additionalProperties": false
            }
          },
          "display": {
            "label": "Database connections",
            "locales": {
              "zh-CN": "数据库连接",
              "zh-TW": "資料庫連線",
              "ja": "データベース接続",
              "ko": "데이터베이스 연결",
              "fr": "Connexions aux bases de données",
              "de": "Datenbankverbindungen",
              "es": "Conexiones de bases de datos",
              "pt-BR": "Conexões de bancos de dados",
              "ru": "Подключения к базам данных",
              "en": "Database connections"
            },
            "icon": "reicon:ui/database"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "database_save_connection",
          "presentation": "details",
          "description": "Create or update a database connection under the session permission policy. Create requires name and engine, plus path for SQLite or host, port, username and database for MySQL/PostgreSQL. If database_connections returns no profiles, create without connection or expected_revision; do not reuse an ID from earlier conversation history. Saving records configuration only and does not create a SQLite file. New connections default to read_only=true; use read_only=false only for requested writes. Update requires connection and expected_revision from database_connections and preserves omitted fields and credentials. Never accept or request passwords; when credentials_required is true, the user supplies them in protected settings. Use the returned ID directly for catalog or SQL tools in this turn. Do not automatically repeat a denied or uncertain save.",
          "contexts": [
            "workspace",
            "database"
          ],
          "handler": {
            "name": "save",
            "operation": "databases.save",
            "result": "saved",
            "parameters": {
              "type": "object",
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "required": [],
              "properties": {
                "connection": {
                  "type": [
                    "string",
                    "null"
                  ],
                  "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{8}(-[0-9a-f]{4}){3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$",
                  "description": "Saved connection ID; omit with expected_revision to create"
                },
                "expected_revision": {
                  "type": [
                    "integer",
                    "null"
                  ],
                  "minimum": 1,
                  "maximum": 9007199254740991
                },
                "name": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "minLength": 1
                },
                "engine": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "sqlite",
                    "mysql",
                    "postgres"
                  ]
                },
                "path": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "minLength": 1,
                  "description": "SQLite file path on the execution Node; relative paths use the captured worktree. Saving does not create the file"
                },
                "host": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "minLength": 1
                },
                "port": {
                  "type": "integer",
                  "minimum": 1,
                  "maximum": 65535
                },
                "username": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "minLength": 1
                },
                "database": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "read_only": {
                  "type": "boolean"
                }
              },
              "allOf": [
                {
                  "if": {
                    "required": [
                      "connection"
                    ],
                    "properties": {
                      "connection": {
                        "type": "string"
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  "then": {
                    "required": [
                      "expected_revision"
                    ],
                    "properties": {
                      "expected_revision": {
                        "type": "integer"
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  "else": {
                    "required": [
                      "name",
                      "engine"
                    ],
                    "properties": {
                      "expected_revision": {
                        "type": "null"
                      }
                    },
                    "allOf": [
                      {
                        "if": {
                          "properties": {
                            "engine": {
                              "const": "sqlite"
                            }
                          }
                        },
                        "then": {
                          "required": [
                            "path"
                          ]
                        },
                        "else": {
                          "required": [
                            "host",
                            "port",
                            "username",
                            "database"
                          ]
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "display": {
            "label": "Save database connection",
            "locales": {
              "zh-CN": "保存数据库连接",
              "zh-TW": "儲存資料庫連線",
              "ja": "データベース接続を保存",
              "ko": "데이터베이스 연결 저장",
              "fr": "Enregistrer la connexion",
              "de": "Datenbankverbindung speichern",
              "es": "Guardar conexión de base de datos",
              "pt-BR": "Salvar conexão de banco de dados",
              "ru": "Сохранить подключение к базе",
              "en": "Save database connection"
            },
            "icon": "reicon:ui/database",
            "input": {
              "summary": {
                "path": "/name",
                "result_path": "/data/name"
              }
            },
            "output": {
              "preview": {
                "parts": [
                  {
                    "value": {
                      "source": "result",
                      "path": "/data/name"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": {
                      "source": "result",
                      "path": "/data/connection"
                    },
                    "format": "json"
                  }
                ],
                "separator": "\n"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "desktop": {
        "entry": "dev.sailry.platform/desktop/main.js",
        "resources": [
          "dev.sailry.platform/desktop/main.js",
          "dev.sailry.platform/desktop/view.js",
          "dev.sailry.platform/desktop/editor-view.js",
          "dev.sailry.platform/desktop/editor.js",
          "dev.sailry.platform/desktop/sql.js",
          "dev.sailry.platform/desktop/catalog.js",
          "dev.sailry.platform/desktop/history.js",
          "dev.sailry.platform/desktop/requests.js",
          "dev.sailry.platform/desktop/locales.js"
        ],
        "navigation": {
          "label": "Databases",
          "locales": {
            "zh-CN": "数据库"
          },
          "icon": "reicon:ui/database"
        },
        "navigation_options": {
          "pinned": true,
          "order": 800,
          "target": "node",
          "details": true
        },
        "conversations": [
          {
            "id": "database",
            "resource": "database",
            "tools": [
              {
                "kind": "plugin",
                "name": "database_catalog"
              },
              {
                "kind": "plugin",
                "name": "database_query"
              },
              {
                "kind": "plugin",
                "name": "database_execute"
              },
              {
                "kind": "plugin",
                "name": "database_connections"
              },
              {
                "kind": "plugin",
                "name": "database_save_connection"
              }
            ],
            "context": "You are the database workspace assistant. Work only with the saved connection exposed by your tools. Use referenced databases and tables as the user's context. Read the connection engine and quoting rules from the tool schema. Use MySQL backticks, and PostgreSQL or SQLite double quotes for identifiers. Use the database argument to select the database rather than assuming cross-database qualification. Inspect catalogs and schema before composing SQL; do not invent table or column names. Use database_query for read-only queries without asking permission. Prefer explicit columns and bounded results. Use database_execute for inserts, updates, deletes, and schema changes: the runtime reviews its exact SQL under the session permission policy. For updates or deletes, inspect matching rows first and use a precise predicate; clarify ambiguous targets with ask_user. Respect the saved connection's read-only setting. Never disable protections, request credentials, or work around a denied operation. Query results already appear in the data grid and SQL log: summarize useful findings instead of repeating large tables. Do not execute a query twice merely to display it. Report errors and uncertain outcomes honestly; never automatically replay a write. Reply in the user's language. Use compact only to manage conversation context. Use database_connections to inspect saved profiles and their revisions. When asked to add or edit a connection, use database_save_connection; never request passwords. SQLite needs no credentials and its returned ID can be used for queries in this turn. If credentials_required is true, ask the user to fill the protected settings field."
          }
        ]
      },
      "instructions": "Use database_connections to inspect saved profiles and their revisions. When no profiles are returned, create a connection without connection or expected_revision; do not reuse IDs from earlier conversation history. When asked to add or edit a connection, use database_save_connection; never request passwords. SQLite needs no credentials and its returned ID can be used in this turn. Saving a connection does not create its file. For a requested new SQLite database, save the connection with read_only=false and use database_execute for the authorized schema write; missing parent directories are created automatically. Explicit writable connection checks can also initialize a missing SQLite file. Do not write an empty file as a workaround or silently change a read-only connection. If credentials_required is true, ask the user to fill the protected settings field.",
      "category": "data",
      "tint": "teal"
    }
  }
}
